Exercise 11.3.5: eliminate i
  eliminating i: 1 lower bound(s), 3 upper bound(s) -> at most 3 new rows
    (i - 1 >= 0)  x  (-i + 29 >= 0)  =>  28 >= 0   [always true, dropped]
    (i - 1 >= 0)  x  (-i + j - 2 >= 0)  =>  j - 3 >= 0
    (i - 1 >= 0)  x  (-i - j + 39 >= 0)  =>  -j + 38 >= 0
(a) result  (vars: i j )
    j - 3 >= 0
    -j + 38 >= 0
  eliminating i: 2 lower bound(s), 2 upper bound(s) -> at most 4 new rows
    (i - 10 >= 0)  x  (-i + 1000 >= 0)  =>  990 >= 0   [always true, dropped]
    (i - 10 >= 0)  x  (-i + j >= 0)  =>  j - 10 >= 0
    (i - j + 9 >= 0)  x  (-i + 1000 >= 0)  =>  -j + 1009 >= 0
    (i - j + 9 >= 0)  x  (-i + j >= 0)  =>  9 >= 0   [always true, dropped]
(b) result  (vars: i j )
    j - 10 >= 0
    -j + 1009 >= 0
  eliminating i: 2 lower bound(s), 3 upper bound(s) -> at most 6 new rows
    (i >= 0)  x  (-i + 99 >= 0)  =>  99 >= 0   [always true, dropped]
    (i >= 0)  x  (-i - j + k >= 0)  =>  -j + k >= 0
    (i >= 0)  x  (-i - j - k + 99 >= 0)  =>  -j - k + 99 >= 0
    (i - j + 99 >= 0)  x  (-i + 99 >= 0)  =>  -j + 198 >= 0
    (i - j + 99 >= 0)  x  (-i - j + k >= 0)  =>  -2*j + k + 99 >= 0
    (i - j + 99 >= 0)  x  (-i - j - k + 99 >= 0)  =>  -2*j - k + 198 >= 0
(c) result  (vars: i j k )
    j >= 0
    -j + k >= 0
    -j - k + 99 >= 0
    -j + 198 >= 0
    -2*j + k + 99 >= 0
    -2*j - k + 198 >= 0
